{
 "lines": [
  {
   "id": "VO-01",
   "start": 0.0,
   "end": 7.683,
   "text": "You just got hired at twenty dollars an hour, you worked eighty hours over two weeks, and your first paycheck should be sixteen hundred dollars."
  },
  {
   "id": "VO-02",
   "start": 7.782,
   "end": 11.028,
   "text": "Then you open it, and it says about thirteen hundred seventy."
  },
  {
   "id": "VO-03",
   "start": 11.177,
   "end": 14.265,
   "text": "Wait, who took two hundred thirty dollars from my check?"
  },
  {
   "id": "VO-04",
   "start": 14.414,
   "end": 20.696,
   "text": "Picture your paycheck as a sixteen hundred dollar pizza, and three people grab a slice before you get a single bite."
  },
  {
   "id": "VO-05",
   "start": 20.795,
   "end": 25.156,
   "text": "Social Security takes six point two percent, ninety-nine dollars and twenty cents."
  },
  {
   "id": "VO-06",
   "start": 25.255,
   "end": 29.901,
   "text": "Medicare grabs one point four five percent, another twenty-three dollars and twenty cents."
  },
  {
   "id": "VO-07",
   "start": 30.001,
   "end": 36.075,
   "text": "Then federal income tax takes about one hundred eight dollars, and in most states, your state grabs a slice too."
  },
  {
   "id": "VO-08",
   "start": 36.473,
   "end": 45.791,
   "text": "So it feels like you just got robbed, but those first two slices fund Social Security and Medicare, and your work history helps decide what you qualify for when you're older."
  },
  {
   "id": "VO-09",
   "start": 45.891,
   "end": 52.717,
   "text": "The income tax slice is just an estimate, and if more was taken than you owe, you get the extra back after you file."
  },
  {
   "id": "VO-10",
   "start": 53.055,
   "end": 61.413,
   "text": "And here's the part nobody tells you, because your boss pays another one hundred twenty-two dollars and forty cents on top, a matching slice you never even see."
  },
  {
   "id": "VO-11",
   "start": 61.81,
   "end": 66.327,
   "text": "You thought your pizza got smaller, but it was actually bigger than you ever saw."
  }
 ],
